the system's trying to

00:45:03.196 --> 00:45:05.320
communicate something that's
other than just

00:45:05.320 --> 00:45:09.470
engagement or fun.

00:45:09.470 --> 00:45:10.758
Was it fun?

00:45:10.758 --> 00:45:11.166
AUDIENCE: Yeah.

00:45:11.166 --> 00:45:11.982
GUEST SPEAKER: Oh, all right.

00:45:11.982 --> 00:45:13.330
Cool.

00:45:13.330 --> 00:45:14.890
Yeah, it's pretty good.

00:45:14.890 --> 00:45:16.090
Thoughts on what it's about?

00:45:16.090 --> 00:45:17.428
I heard a couple people
be like, drugs.

00:45:17.428 --> 00:45:19.212
AUDIENCE: It's definitely
drugs.

00:45:19.212 --> 00:45:21.806
I saw tons of analogies.

00:45:21.806 --> 00:45:24.250
GUEST SPEAKER: Yeah, it's
kind of like drugs.

00:45:24.250 --> 00:45:24.670
AUDIENCE: Or love.

00:45:24.670 --> 00:45:25.680
Or both.

00:45:25.680 --> 00:45:27.370
AUDIENCE: Love is a drug.

00:45:27.370 --> 00:45:29.410
AUDIENCE: Your relationship
versus whatever you're trying

00:45:29.410 --> 00:45:30.790
to do for your career.

00:45:30.790 --> 00:45:32.040
GUEST SPEAKER: Yeah.

00:45:33.655 --> 00:45:36.570
I think it's like the
ultimate MIT game.

00:45:36.570 --> 00:45:41.530
If I told you that this was his
daughter, would it change

00:45:41.530 --> 00:45:44.050
