her any money.

00:46:34.650 --> 00:46:38.640
Because she had no money,
she dies [INAUDIBLE].

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:42.120
GUEST SPEAKER: So I think
this is a really--

00:46:42.120 --> 00:46:43.360
AUDIENCE: What did they say,
it's a game about motivation?

00:46:43.360 --> 00:46:45.660
GUEST SPEAKER: It is, yeah.

00:46:45.660 --> 00:46:47.770
AUDIENCE: Or she
OD'd on drugs.

00:46:47.770 --> 00:46:48.350
GUEST SPEAKER: It's free.

00:46:48.350 --> 00:46:50.320
If you just Google-search
Gravitation Jason Rohrer,

00:46:50.320 --> 00:46:51.600
you'll find the links to it.

00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:53.510
You'll find his artist
statement, which I think is

00:46:53.510 --> 00:46:55.070
really good to read.

00:46:55.070 --> 00:46:57.850
Again, with John Sharp's point
about declare your

00:46:57.850 --> 00:46:58.400
intentionality.

00:46:58.400 --> 00:47:02.370
Whatever you say what game's
about is important.

00:47:02.370 --> 00:47:05.800
I think this qualifies, at
least for me, as art.

00:47:05.800 --> 00:47:11.230
It's doing things that I see
other piece of art doing.

00:47:11.230 --> 00:47:12.710
GUEST SPEAKER: OK, so
Paolo Pedercini--

00:47:12.710 --> 00:47:13.540
how many over time?

00:47:13.540 --> 00:47:14.610
